    <string name="contrib_tips">Get very close and fill the frame with one part per photo: leaf top, leaf underside, flower, fruit (whole and cut open), stem or bark, seedling, then the whole plant. Sharp, in daylight, several angles. 3 or more per stage is ideal. Never touch or taste a plant you don’t know.</string>
